/target
crates/*/target
# `ref_data/` is NOT ignored: a test fixture nobody can regenerate is not a
# reproducibility claim. burn-gdn2's bit-exact fixture is committed (the
# exception below) and burn-sct's is wanted the same way once its generator
# exists — see crates/burn-gdn2/TEST-AUDIT.md.
**/*.bin
!crates/burn-gdn2/tests/ref_data.bin
# The f64 reference fixtures, same reason and one more: `tests/ref_f64.rs` must
# run in CI without Python or NumPy present at all, so the expected values have
# to be bytes in the tree. `ref_f64.bin` is the layer's output;
# `ref_f64_faults.bin` is the other side of its margin, and a margin asserted
# against data nobody can regenerate is not a margin.
!crates/burn-gdn2/tests/ref_f64.bin
!crates/burn-gdn2/tests/ref_f64_faults.bin
Cargo.lock.bak
.bulba/
